      {
        "section_id": "nav:jamieson-fausset-brown:PSA.132:P:psa-132-1-18-the-writer-perhaps-solomon-compare-psa-132-8-9-after-relating-dav",
        "navigation_id": "PSA.132:P:psa-132-1-18-the-writer-perhaps-solomon-compare-psa-132-8-9-after-relating-dav",
        "scope": "passage",
        "role": "passage_overview",
        "title": "Psa 132:1-18 . The writer, perhaps Solomon (compare Psa 132:8 , 9 ), after relating David's pious zeal for God's service, pleads for the fulfilment of the promise ( 2Sa 7:16 ), which, providing for a perpetuation of David's kingdom, involved that of God's right worship and the establishment of the greater and spiritual kingdom of David's greater Son. Of Him and His kingdom both the temple and its worship, and the kings and kingdom of Judah, were types. The congruity of such a topic with the tenor of this series of Psalms is obvious."
      }
    ],
